+# CONTRACT — Versioned Document Store with Structural Merge
+
+Definition of done. Every box must pass via `npm test`, `npm run build`, `npm run lint`.
+
+## Documents (CRUD)
+- [ ] `create(id, content)` stores a new doc -> `get(id)` returns deep-equal content
+- [ ] `create` throws if id already exists on current branch
+- [ ] `get(id)` throws if doc never existed
+- [ ] `get(id)` throws if doc was deleted
+- [ ] `get` returns a deep clone (mutating the returned object does not affect store)
+- [ ] `create` stores a deep clone (mutating the input object afterward does not affect store)
+- [ ] `update(id, content)` replaces content -> `get` returns new content
+- [ ] `update` throws if doc doesn't exist
+- [ ] `update` stores a deep clone of input
+- [ ] `delete(id)` removes doc -> subsequent `get` throws
+- [ ] `delete` throws if doc doesn't exist
+
+## Version History
+- [ ] `create` produces a version; `getHistory` length == 1 after create
+- [ ] each `update` adds a version (chronological, oldest first)
+- [ ] every version has unique `id`, a numeric `timestamp`, and full `content`
+- [ ] `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns content at that version (deep clone)
+- [ ] `getVersion` throws on unknown versionId
+- [ ] `getHistory` content reflects the state at each point (not all the latest)
+- [ ] `getHistory` returns deep clones (mutation-safe)
+
+## Branching
+- [ ] default branch is `"main"`; `getBranch()` returns `"main"` initially
+- [ ] `createBranch(name)` branches from current branch's current state
+- [ ] `createBranch(name, fromBranch)` branches from the named branch
+- [ ] `createBranch` throws if branch already exists
+- [ ] `createBranch`/`switchBranch` throw if fromBranch/name does not exist
+- [ ] `switchBranch` changes active branch; CRUD applies to it
+- [ ] `listBranches()` returns all branch names
+- [ ] changes on one branch are invisible on another
+- [ ] a branch sees the documents that existed at branch creation time
+
+## Merging (three-way)
+- [ ] merge with no changes on either side -> no-op, `applied: true`, no conflicts
+- [ ] only-source changed a doc/field -> change taken, applied, no conflict (fast-forward style)
+- [ ] only-ours changed -> source has nothing new -> applied, ours kept
+- [ ] both changed DIFFERENT fields of same doc -> merged union, no conflict, applied
+- [ ] both changed SAME field to SAME value -> no conflict, applied
+- [ ] both changed SAME field to DIFFERENT values -> conflict, `applied: false`, branch unchanged
+- [ ] conflict reports `documentId`, dot-path (e.g. `a.b.c`), base, ours, theirs
+- [ ] nested object fields merge recursively; conflict path is dot-separated
+- [ ] different documents changed on different branches -> merge cleanly, no conflict
+- [ ] new doc added only on source -> appears in merged result, applied
+- [ ] doc deleted on one side, untouched on other -> deletion applied, no conflict
+- [ ] `merged` always contains the result; conflicts resolved ours-wins in `merged`
+- [ ] when conflicts exist, current branch state is unchanged (verify via get)
+- [ ] when applied, current branch reflects merged content
+- [ ] re-merge after a prior merge uses the updated merge base (no spurious conflicts)
+- [ ] arrays are treated as atomic values (equal arrays = no change; differing = conflict if both change)
